-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",408,{
[13025]="7000AE6C\n1\tTalk to Billina\tBillina is in the yard at Sandson's Farm. Billina wishes to speak with you.\n2\tVisit Brownlock's coop\030Visit Maggot's coop\030Visit Cotton's coop\tThere are chicken coops at Brownlock's Farm on the road east and slightly north to Needlehole, Cotton's Farm to the east in Bywater, and Farmer Maggot's farm to the east and south along the Brandywine River. Billina has asked you to warn the other chicken coops in the Shire about the threat of wolves.\n",
[13026]="7004799B\n1\tDefeat foes in the Slag-hills (total: 20)\tMany foes can be found in and around the Slag-hills. You should defeat foes within the Slag-hills.\n2\tReturn to Candúr\tYou should return to Candúr, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.\n",
[13027]="70037ACE\n1\tThe Orc that slew Ordgar lies next to him, north of Grimslade in the Westfold. You should speak with the dying Orc.\t\n2\tCompleted\tYou have avenged Ordgar, whose death was needless. Fewer Orcs now haunt the Westfold.\n",
[13028]="7001D136\n1\tCollect tokens of bondage from morvul-slaves (total: 10)\tMorvul-slaves can be found in Dannenglor, to the north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks. Puiguil has asked you to defeat many morvul-slaves in Dannenglor and collect the tokens of bondage that can be found on them.\n2\tTalk to Puiguil at the Haunted Inn\tPuiguil is at the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood, south of Dannenglor. You should speak with Puiguil and bring him the tokens of the mervyl's allegiance to their family.\n",
[13029]="70027B02\n1\tTalk to Barkh\tBarkh manages the kitchens in the south-west wall of the cavern beneath Isengard. Your overseer wants you to report to the kitchens beneath Isengard for work.\n2\tClean up piles of slop in the kitchens (total: 6)\tPiles of slop litter the floor of the kitchens beneath Isengard. Barkh has given you a rag and the unenviable task of cleaning up after the Uruk-hai.\n3\tUse the slop bucket in the kitchens to squeeze out the dirty rag\tThe slop bucket is in the kitchens. Barkh wants you to squeeze out the rag you used to clean up the slop into the slop bucket in the kitchens.\n4\tReturn the dirty rag to Barkh\tBarkh is waiting to speak to you in the kitchens beneath Isengard.\n5\tClean up piles of slop in the kitchens (total: 6)\tThere is still slop to be cleaned up in the kitchens beneath Isengard.\n6\tUse the slop bucket in the kitchens to squeeze out the dirty rag\tThe slop bucket is in the kitchens. Barkh wants you to squeeze out the rag you used to clean up the slop into the slop bucket in the kitchens.\n7\tReturn the dirty rag to Barkh\tBarkh is in the kitchens beneath Isengard, waiting to speak to you.\n8\tGet some slop from the slop bucket in the kitchens\tBarkh wants you to get some slop from the slop bucket in the kitchens and bring it to the bucket in the dungeons. The entrance to the dungeons is in the north-west wall of the main cavern.\n9\tTalk to Baldgar in the dungeon\tOne of the prisoners has tried to get your attention. You should talk to him.\n10\tTalk to your Uruk-hai overseer\tYour Uruk-hai overseer wants to talk to you.\n",
[13030]="70028CFA\n1\tDefeat Mange-rider\tThe chief of the Warg-riders is somewhere within the Howling Caverns. You should defeat Mange-rider, the chief of the Warg-riders.\n2\tTalk to Goronu\tGoronu can be found outside of the Howling Caverns in Pren Gwydh. You should inform Goronu that you have defeated the chief of the Warg-riders.\n3\tTalk to Luned in Galtrev\tLuned is in Galtrev, waiting anxiously to hear of the vicious Wargs that roam the landscape of late. You should tell Luned that you have brought down many Wargs and their riders and hopefully rooted out the source of the evil that entered these lands.\n",
[13031]="70058CF1\n1\tSet traps on the outskirts of Khadâsh-gâra (total: 8)\tKhadâsh-gâra can be found in eastern Elderslade. Bráthur has asked you to set traps on the outskirts of Khadâsh-gâra.\n2\tTalk to Bráthur\tBráthur can be found at Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade. You have set many traps on the outskirts of Khadâsh-gâra. You should return to Bráthur.\n",
[13032]="7001BBA3\n1\tCollect wolf-pelts from the Darkrage wolves (total: 12)\tDarkrage wolves can be found throughout the Dourstocks and in Audaghaim. The Ranger Prestadír has asked you to collect the pelts of several of the evil wolves that harass the Malledhrim-guards.\n2\tBring the wolf-pelts to Prestadír\tPrestadír can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, near the abandoned village of Audaghaim. You should bring the wolf-pelts you have collected to Prestadír, for he wishes to examine them.\n",
[13033]="70060D85\n1\tCollect stink-bombs (total: 10)\tFredegar Bolger has been making and storing stink-bombs around Nobottle, should the need arise. You should collect all the stink-bombs for Fredegar Bolger.\n2\tThrow stink-bombs at Lotho's Bounders (total: 4)\tLotho's Bounders can be found in Yondershire. You should throw stink bombs at Lotho's Bounders.\n3\tTalk to Fredegar in Nobottle\tFredegar Bolger can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should talk to Fredegar Bolger.\n4\tTalk to Fredegar in Nobottle\tFredegar Bolger can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should talk to Fredegar Bolger.\n",
[13034]="7002E531\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Hereswith\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13035]="7002E529\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Fréamar\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13036]="7002E52C\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Hereswith\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13037]="7002E530\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Edgal\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13038]="7002E538\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Oseg\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13039]="70043058\n1\tStart smoky fires (total: 4)\tThere are wooded areas west of the Harlond and the road leading up to it. Dindal has suggested that you start smoky fires at old camp-fire sites in wooded areas near the Harlond, in order to lure Orc raiding parties to you in small groups.\n2\tTalk to Dindal\tDindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui. You should return to Dindal and let him know that his plan worked.\n",
[13040]="7004CE1E\n1\tFind the smugglers' hideout\tThe smugglers' hideout can be found in the Lake-town underbelly. You should find the smugglers' hideout.\n2\tTalk to the door guard\tThe smugglers' hideout can be found in the Lake-town underbelly. You should talk to the door guard.\n3\tSeize the smugglers' leader, Skótmun\tThe smugglers' hideout can be found in the Lake-town underbelly. You should seize the smugglers' leader, Skótmun.\n4\tTalk to Dagrun\tDagrun can be found in the Trade Commission Headquarters. You should talk to Dagrun.\n",
[13041]="7003EDBD\n1\tDefeat spiders in the Snares before the time runs out (total: 8)\tSpiders can be found in the Snares, south of Esteldín in the Kingsfell. You should defeat spiders as quickly as you can, before the time runs out. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have swiftly defeated a number of the Kingsfell spiders in the Snares, helping to make the area near Esteldín safer and free of the influence of evil.\n",
[13042]="7005297B\n1\tEnter Ylgraf\tYlgraf can be found on the northern edge of the Beorning-lands. You should defeat wargs and burn animal carcasses found at Ylgraf.\n2\tDefeat wargs at Ylgraf (total: 10)\030Burn animal carcasses (total: 10)\tYlgraf can be found on the northern edge of the Beorning-lands. You should defeat wargs and burn animal carcasses found at Ylgraf.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated wargs and burned animal carcasses.\n",
[13043]="70052B16\n1\tTalk to Atta\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. Atta has offered to tell you the tale of the night he encountered Úbil the Snatcher.\n2\tTalk to Atta\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. You have heard the tale of Atta's encounter with Úbil the Snatcher. You should talk to Atta.\n",
[13044]="7002C601\n1\tVisit the goats south-west of Magla and search for what frightened him\030Visit the goats north of Magla and search for what frightened him\tGoats mill about the Wailing Hills in their enclosures to the north and to the south-west of Magla. Magla had a frightening experience near the goats of the Wailing Hills and wants you to see if there is any sign of what so frightened him.\n2\tTalk to Magla\tMagla is near the two goat enclosures in the Wailing Hills. You visited the goats milling about the Wailing Hills but found no sign of the creature that so frightened Magla.\n",
[13045]="70035217\n1\tFind out what caused the strange weather to appear in Byre Tor\tStrange weather has cropped up in Byre Tor. Something is wrong....\n2\tHead North-east away from Byre Tor, to the tallest peak\tA tall craggy peak stands to the north-east. You should head to the high peak, away from Byre Tor, where your vantage point will be better.\n3\tEnter the cave\tA cave full of grim-looking people stands in the High Knolls north of Byre Tor. You should speak with one of the people.\n",
[13046]="70037CCC\n1\tBury dead Rohirrim\tThe bodies of Rohirrim soldiers litter the Fords of Isen. You should bury many of the soldiers, for they deserve a better passing than to rot in the footprints of the enemy host.\n2\tBury dead Rohirrim (total: 10)\tThe bodies of Rohirrim soldiers litter the Fords of Isen. You should bury many of the soldiers, for they deserve a better passing than to rot in the footprints of the enemy host.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have buried enough bodies for now, for sadly there will be many more before the night is through.\n",
[13047]="700661E0\n1\tTalk to Halnith at Nendath\tBruidis has asked you to check on Halnith. Halnith guards the beacon Nendath, which stands to the east of Tadrent.\n",
[13048]="7006656D\n1\tDefeat Corsairs in Tungobel (total: 8)\030Collect pillaged supplies (total: 6)\tErchar is worried that a camp of lingering Corsairs are stealing supplies meant for Parth Rest. The Corsair camp can be found west of Dol Brannor.\n2\tTalk to Herion at Parth Rest\tYou should deliver the pillaged supplies to Herion at Parth Rest. Parth Rest can be found to the south-west of Dol Brannor.\n",
[13049]="7000111B\n1\tElladan and Elrohir are at Thorenhad, east and north of Narlinn's camp. The ruins may be found by following the road eastward to the white marker stone and taking the northward path to the bluff. Narlinn has asked you to bring news of the trolls and the Shadow-wolf to Elladan and Elrohir, the sons of Elrond.\t\n",
[13050]="70060014\n1\tDefeat the Stone-giants, Ramthol and Víthinga\tHlídborg can be found in south eastern Câr Bronach. You should defeat the Stone-giants, Ramthol and Víthinga, found at Hlídborg.\n2\tDefeat the Stone-giant, Ramthol\030Defeat the Stone-giant, Víthinga\tHlídborg can be found in south eastern Câr Bronach. You should defeat the Stone-giants, Ramthol and Víthinga, found at Hlídborg.\n",
[13051]="700304B0\n1\tEnter the Easterling encampment of Jóshkhin Orda\tThe Sorcerer's Council resides in five towers throughout the large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr. You should defeat each of the members of the Sorcerer's Council.\n2\tDefeat a member of the Sorcerer's Council (total: 3)\tThe Sorcerer's Council resides in five towers throughout the large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr. You should defeat each of the members of the Sorcerer's Council.\n3\tReturn to Guthferth at North-torr\tSergeant Guthferth stands guard at North-torr, just north of the city of Floodwend in the Wold. You should speak with Guthferth.\n",
[13052]="700715A8\n1\tSpeak with the leader of the warband in Ingar-garâsh\tSpeak with the leader of the warband in Ingar-garâsh. Ingar-garâsh can be found in Kighân to the south-west of Sormedân, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[13053]="700190F7\n1\tFind the source of the strange goo\tThe highest concentration of the creatures can be found near Gabil-Munz, the great structure to the south-west. Hasta has asked you to find the source of the strange substance and bring back a pure sample of the stuff for further study.\n2\tBring the sample to Hasta\tHasta is at the Rotting Cellar in the Water-works, north-east from Gabil-munz. Now that you have found the source of the strange substance and extracted another sample, you should bring it to Hasta for more extensive study. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[13054]="70027E89\n1\tLook for the Dragon-clan's rallying point nearby\tAccording to the map you captured from the Dragon-clan invaders, a major rallying point lies somewhere nearby. You should see if you can find the rallying point and look for any signs of the Dragon-clan. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tReturn to Guto at his encampment\tGuto can be found at his encampment in the southern fields of Trum Dreng. You should tell Guto what you saw when you scouted the encampment.\n",
[13055]="7002EE5C\n1\tDiscover the source of the madness in the Wódfen\t\n2\tYou should scour the Wódfen for clues to the source of the madness that has overcome the wildlife there.\t\n3\tFind the draug-cave\tThe entrance to the draugar's cave must be somewhere in the Wódfen. You should seek the entrance to the draugar's cave.\n4\tDefeat draugar in Byrgenstow (total: 15)\tDraugar can be found in their cave, as well as in the Wódfen at night. You should purge the Wódfen of the draug-threat.\n",
[13056]="70030C72\n1\tFind the source of the mist\tThe source of the mist can likely be found to the west of Oldheart. You should search for the source to the ugly-looking mist that hangs above the trees.\n2\tSearch for corpses (total: 3)\030Search for piles of slop (total: 3)\030Search for rubbish (total: 3)\tThe Orcs and Uruks passing through this area have left filth all around the edges of this poor little pond. You should investigate what manner of filth pollutes this water.\n3\tSearch for the bird around the pond\tYou suspect that the little bird sought by Oldheart inhaled the fumes of this foetid pond, and likely died of the poisons. You should search for the little bird.\n4\tCompleted\tYou have found a great deal of filth from the slovenly horde of Orcs and Uruks who have gathered temporarily in this sector of Fangorn. This poor pond is polluted beyond recognition. The water is not water, but poison. The servants of the White Hand are cruel in even their carelessness.\n",
})
